#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:64
msgid ""
"Mattermost provides a set of :doc:`pre-built plugins </integrations-guide"
"/popular-integrations>` that require no coding to install, configure, and"
" use. These plugins are installed and managed entirely through the System"
" Console, where you can enable, configure, and customize settings without"
" any development work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:66
msgid "Pre-built plugins available for no-code integration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:71
msgid "Custom-Built Plugins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:73
#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:124
msgid "**Technical complexity:** :ref:`Pro-code <pro-code>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:75
msgid ""
":ref:`Building custom plugins <integrations-guide/plugins:custom-built "
"plugins>` are the most comprehensive way to add new features and "
"customization to self-hosted Mattermost deployments. Custom plugins are "
"ideal for customers wanting to change the behavior of the Mattermost "
"server, desktop, and web apps without forking the core codebase to suit "
"their organization’s needs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:77
msgid ""
"Building a custom plugin is a **software development** task, using ``Go``"
" for the server-side functionality and optionally ``TypeScript/React`` "
"for UI components."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:80
msgid "Webhooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:82
msgid ""
"Learn more about :doc:`Mattermost webhooks </integrations-guide/webhook-"
"integrations>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:85
msgid "Incoming Webhooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:89
msgid ""
":doc:`Incoming webhooks </integrations-guide/incoming-webhooks>` allow "
"external applications to post messages into Mattermost channels and "
"direct messages. They are a simple way to receive notifications and data "
"from other services in real-time and require only basic setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:91
msgid ""
"Additionally, Mattermost webhook payloads are :ref:`fully compatible "
"<integrations-guide/incoming-webhooks:slack compatibility>` with Slack’s "
"webhook format to make migration easier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:94
msgid "Outgoing Webhooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:96
#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:115
msgid "**Technical complexity:** :ref:`Low-code <low-code>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:98
msgid ""
":doc:`Outgoing webhooks </integrations-guide/outgoing-webhooks>` allow "
"Mattermost to send messages and trigger actions in external applications "
"when specific keywords are typed in channels. They are a straightforward "
"way to connect Mattermost conversations to other services and automate "
"responses. Outgoing webhooks require no coding to configure in "
"Mattermost. Some light coding is required to parse the request from the "
"external service and format a JSON response payload."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:101
msgid "Slash Commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:103
msgid ""
"Learn more about :doc:`Mattermost slash commands </integrations-guide"
"/slash-commands>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:106
msgid "Built-In Slash Commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:110
msgid ""
"Out-of-the-box :doc:`built-in slash commands </integrations-guide/built-"
"in-slash-commands>` enable command line interaction with users, channels,"
" and conversations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:113
msgid "Custom Slash Commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:117
msgid ""
"You can create :ref:`custom slash commands <integrations-guide/slash-"
"commands:custom slash commands>` that run preconfigured commands that can"
" return a response, such as plain text, rich message content, interactive"
" buttons or forms, directly into a channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:119
msgid ""
"Mattermost's slash command format is Slack compatible, so you can easily "
"migrate your commands from Slack."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:122
msgid "RESTful API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:126
msgid ""
"With :doc:`Mattermost's RESTful API </integrations-guide/restful-api>`, "
"you have full developer control for automation, bots, and integrations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:129
msgid "Build and Automate Workflows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:133
msgid ""
"In addition to direct tool integrations, Mattermost can be part of larger"
" automated workflows across your integrated services. Automate multi-step"
" processes across Mattermost and other systems, often with no coding "
"required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:136
msgid "No-code Automation Platforms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:138
msgid ""
"Platforms like n8n, Zapier, and Make provide powerful visual editors that"
" support thousands of connected tools, with triggers and actions that "
"integrate Mattermost to external services, enabling teams to build "
"complex workflows without writing code. Admins migrating from tools like "
"Slack Workflow Builder can recreate familiar automations in Mattermost "
"using these platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:140
msgid ""
"Learn more about additional :doc:`no-code automation options "
"</integrations-guide/no-code-automation>` available in Mattermost."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:143
msgid "Mattermost Playbooks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:145
msgid ""
":doc:`Mattermost Playbooks </end-user-guide/workflow-automation>` lets "
"you define and execute repeatable processes without any coding. Playbooks"
" are often used for incident response, onboarding checklists, or any "
"workflow that involves multiple steps, owners, and notifications. "
"Playbooks have integration points you can use to trigger actions, and "
"they can work in conjunction with plugins, making them a powerful no-code"
" automation tool for orchestrating both human and system actions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/integrations-guide/integrations-guide-index.rst:147
msgid ""
"Learn more about using :doc:`Playbooks </end-user-guide/workflow-"
"automation>`."
msgstr ""

